{
  "//": "Every dynamic folder under app/, classified by what its [segment] can hold (owner 2026-09-30, inbox #91). 'text' means a person typed it (a player name, a team name, a code) and it can carry spaces, symbols and glyphs: links to it go through lib/routes.ts and every read of it goes through readSegment(). The other kinds are generated by the site (Django slugify is ASCII only, tokens are hex, ids are numbers). scripts/check-route-segments.mjs fails on a folder missing here, a key naming no folder, a raw link to a 'text' prefix, and a 'text' read that skips readSegment. A new dynamic route is classified here in the same commit.",
  "routes": {
